  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is RNA multiprofile with scvi_n200 (0.650 avgpool, 0.653 transformer; F1 supports), while PCA is lower and image-only ResNet is weak. scgpt is untested, so there is uncertainty about RNA representation. config_008 tests scgpt under the same multiprofile/avgpool setting, isolating the encoder effect without adding fusion or relying on the tiny transformer advantage. This is a simple, high-value extension of the promising RNA direction, can improve the current best baseline, and clarifies whether encoder choice matters before investing in multimodal fusion."
}

